an feeling  like it's an obligation like she did the  first time this fake reality does break  apart a little of course as geralt tries  to reach through to siri and it's only  on for a moment but at one point  malsak's face suddenly flipped to an  image of the doppler assassin who killed  the druid in the first season and took  on his form until revealing his true  nature to siri and dara  the netflix show's first season already  introduced some magical signs that are  popular in the witcher games and we also  get to see some more cool ones in season  two so when geralt is battling the  brooks as piercing screams in the first  episode he casts a quen sign which forms  a defensive shield against the sonic  waves he also appears to cast it later  to create a protective barrier when the  myriapod attacks him in the woods though  this might be the alternate heliotrope  sign which only protects against a  single physical attack and the way  geralt lights up his blade could be  either the igni sign or a temporary fire  rune which he can apply to his sword in  the witcher 2 game and in the final  battle with the deathless mother and the  basilisks geralt casts an urden sign  which can block and slow down monsters  from entering an area protected by the  sign he uses this so he can attempt to  negotiate with voloth and get through to  siri without having to fight the  basilisks at the same time  geralt's mentioned to siri of a  nightmare about an overly friendly rock  troll appears to be an easter egg to the  somewhat chatty trolls in the witcher 3  game can we talk ziggy you like talk me  with there's a big clue you might have  missed a season two's twist ending that  siri's father dooney is still alive but  just before we get to that if you'd like  to try out another immersive gaming  world like the witcher check out  mecharina who've kindly sponsored this  video it's a great low stress  multiplayer combat game where you can  fight with friends or team up with them  in a